    description: 'Blue Cross MN experimental / investigative classification: evidence addressing the published test',
    severity: 'flag',
    citation: 'Blue Cross MN determines experimental, investigative, or unproven status on a preponderance of evidence across three published tests: final approval from the appropriate government regulatory agency where required, consensus opinions in relevant scientific and medical literature, peer-reviewed journals, or clinical-trial and technology-assessment reports, and consensus opinions of national and local providers in the applicable specialty. Its contract definition turns on FDA approval for the relevant indication and on proof of effect on health outcomes outside the research setting. <https://www.bluecrossmn.com/sites/default/files/DAM/2023-05/bcbsmn-provider-policy-and-procedure-manual.pdf>',
