    citation: 'Louisiana Blue concurrent review nurses review new admissions and continued-care cases before the end of an approved length of stay, and a nurse with the medical director reviews the information provided to document the medical necessity for continued stay, deciding within one business day. In-state acute care facilities reimbursed by anything other than per diem are not required to perform concurrent review at all; they submit the initial clinical information and, at discharge, the disposition and diagnosis. <https://providers.lablue.com/-/media/Files/Providers/Professional%20Provider%20Office%20Manual/2025/Prof%20Manual%202025%20Section%204%20pdf.pdf>',
